feed/actions.ts:336-339: `// Delete image files
  await deletePostImages(post.images);

  await prisma.post.delete({ where: { id: postId } });`. If prisma.post.delete throws (transient pgbouncer/DB failure, timeout), the R2 objects are already gone (delImage is not undoable) but the post survives: every reader sees the post with dead image URLs forever, and re-clicking delete is the author's only remedy (which does work — delImage is best-effort on missing objects — but nothing tells them to). The declinePhoto/adminRemovePhoto/purge paths all order row-first or row-in-transaction; deletePost is the outlier.
